{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GHzdur6scqXBUneG2VjT1n","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Anchor R&D Surface v10 â€” \"Live Handoff & Boneyard\" â€” Execution Log\n2\t\n3\t> Foreman appends per-wave EXECUTE / ADVERSARIAL-REVIEW / FIX / JUDGE history here.\n4\t> Frozen design: `MASTER-PLAN.md`. Build plan: `IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md`.\n5\t> Branch `foreman/rnd-surface-v10` off master `b33c74a` (v9 merged `9baabf0` + the\n6\t> Buildâ†’Planning tie commit). Baseline at branch cut: GREEN 1068, 1 skipped.\n7\t\n8\t<!-- Foreman writes below this line. -->\n9\t\n10\t## Wave 1 â€” Paste-NOT-submit handoff substrate (backend) â€” âœ… GREEN (2 iters)\n11\t\n12\t- **EXECUTE.** Added `paste_prompt=` to `terminal_session.start_session` (phase-1 seed still submitted; the prompt recorded as `pending_paste`, not written); `_flush_pending_paste` writes it to the PTY unsent, once, after the greet; wired into `attach`/`read_since`. `session_registry._normalize` + `update_session` allow-list gain `pending_paste:str=\"\"` / `paste_flushed:bool=False`. New `tests/test_pending_paste_v10.py`.\n13\t- **GATE 1.** Full suite GREEN 1080/1 â€” but review flagged the gate did not actually verify \"after the greet\".\n14\t- **REVIEW (2 independent, refute).** Both corroborated: **BLOCKER** premature flush â€” the greet marker is a literal substring of the echoed seed, so the paste fired before the model greeted (concrete repro, zero model greet); **MAJOR** double-paste TOCTOU under `ThreadingHTTPServer`; **MINOR** no newline strip (a `NEXT-PROMPT.md` ending in `\\n` would auto-submit).\n15\t- **FIX iter 1.** Greet detection now = marker occurrences **beyond** the seed's own (`base = seed_text.count(marker)`; flush iff buffer count > base) â€” non-vacuous (the \"no premature flush\" test fails against the old logic). Double-paste closed by a compare-and-set under the reentrant `paths.WRITE_LOCK` (claim `paste_flushed=True` before the PTY write; loser no-ops). `pending.rstrip(\"\\r\\n\")` before write. Tests grew 8â†’11 (added no-premature-flush, newline-strip, 2-thread concurrency).\n16\t- **GATE 2 (orchestrator-run, of record).** `python -m pytest -q` â†’ **GREEN 1083 passed, 1 skipped**. Closure verified in code (`terminal_session.py:547-575`).\n17\t- **VERDICT: GO.** Commit scoped (terminal_session.py, session_registry.py, tests/test_pending_paste_v10.py).\n18\t\n19\t## Wave 2 â€” Both-artifact advance + paste-in-panel (UI) â€” âœ… GREEN (awaiting John's UI sign-off)\n20\t\n21\t- **EXECUTE.** `handoff.build_next_stage_prompt` (reviewable prompt, real doc paths) + `write_next_prompt` â†’ `NEXT-PROMPT.md`. `terminal_session.auto_advance_planning_to_build` (+ reconcile_and_advance + finish_to_build path) now start the next session with `paste_prompt=` (Wave-1 pending paste, UNSENT) instead of the auto-submitted seed; both artifacts written. `/api/rnd/advance_session` (researchâ†’plan) delivers the paste + records the stage edge + `_flashPendingPasteHint`. Mockup `_mockups/advance_paste.html`. New tests + Playwright `test_advance_paste_ui_v10.py`.\n22\t- **GATE 1.** Found 3 regressions in `test_handoff_docs_v8.py` (the build-seed assertions â€” the task content correctly moved seedâ†’paste). **FIX:** relocated those 3 tests to assert the real paths + Foreman in `pending_paste` + `NEXT-PROMPT.md` (plan-cited per D6; strictly stronger, none weakened). Playwright header test was case (a) â€” header correctly shows Foreman.\n23\t- **REVIEW (2 independent, refute).** Corroborated (â‰¥2): the Playwright POSITIVE token (`\"Crucible\"`) also appears in the echoed phase-1 seed â†’ non-discriminating; no RENDERED negative for not-auto-submitted (v4 standard gap). Plus: `finish_to_build` marks planning DONE without `kill` â†’ docs not persisted â†’ build checkout can lack the paths `NEXT-PROMPT.md` references (North-Star hole). Plus LOW: redundant \"Load the skill\" in the reviewable paste.\n24\t- **FIX iter 1.** (1) UI test now asserts a paste-ONLY token (`research/run-1/REPORT.md`, absent from the seed) is visible in the xterm DOM + a rendered negative (cursor stays on the paste row; no submitted row below) â€” **proven non-vacuous by sabotaging `_flush_pending_paste` with `\\n` (test FAILED), then reverting**; added a non-Playwright DOM positive+negative leg. (2) `finish_to_build` now `capture_session_docs` (persist+commit to main, NO reap â€” tile stays) BEFORE advancing, so the build worktree contains the docs; new test asserts `(build_wt/impl).is_file()` + main commit. (3) `handoff.clean_paste_opener` strips the redundant load-prefix from the paste only (\"With Foreman loaded, â€¦\"); seeds unchanged; skill name + paths + read-first preserved. (Recovered from an accidental `git checkout` of terminal_session.py â€” reconstruction verified by the full gate.)\n25\t- **GATE 2 (orchestrator-run, of record).** `python -m pytest -q` â†’ **GREEN 1094 passed, 1 skipped**.\n26\t- **VERDICT: GO â€” committed to branch (453f687).** âœ… **John signed off on the screenshot 2026-06-17 (\"carry on\").** Wave 2 done.\n27\t\n28\t## Wave 3 â€” Grass workbench: two independently-toggleable terminals (UI) â€” âœ… GREEN (awaiting John's UI sign-off)\n29\t\n30\t- **EXECUTE.** Replaced the single shared grass `.term-host` with TWO per-lane `.gterm` hosts (research + plan), each with its own toggle (â–¾/â–¸); `toggleGrassTerminal` opens/collapses one independently; collapse hides the host but keeps the session LIVE (never kills). `develop_grass_idea` already supports one session per lane â€” no backend change. Mockup `_mockups/grass_two_terminals.html`. New DOM + Playwright tests.\n31\t- **GATE 1.** Full suite GREEN 1099.\n32\t- **REVIEW (2 independent, refute) â€” split verdict, resolved by OBSERVED evidence.** Reviewer A: **BLOCKER** â€” `saveGrassRefinement` reads an undeclared `panel` (anchor_gui.py:4215; the rework deleted its binding) â†’ `ReferenceError` on every Save; missed by the suite because no test clicks Save. Reviewer B: GO, claimed \"no crash\". Judge read the code â†’ A confirmed correct. Both flagged (â‰¥2): single Save button is lane-ambiguous with two terminals. Reviewer B's continued pass also surfaced a **flaky WS/SSE teardown race** (`WinError 10053`) under full-suite load.\n33\t- **FIX iter 1.** (1) Restored the `#grassPanel` container lookup â€” Save raises no console error + flips the row status; **proven non-vacuous** (re-introducing the bug fails the new test). (2) Save-refinement is now **per-lane** â€” each terminal has its own `data-save-lane` Save targeting that lane's session. (3) Removed inert `.tpane` dead CSS. (4) Added the missing Save-refinement coverage (DOM positive+negative + Playwright: no console error + status flip).\n34\t- **FLAKE HARDENING (deterministic-gate fix).** Product: `_is_benign_disconnect` (tight set: BrokenPipeError/ConnectionResetError/ConnectionAbortedError + OSError winerror 10053/10054) now makes the SSE/WS/HTTP write paths + `do_GET`/`do_POST` return cleanly on client disconnect (correct production behavior â€” a browser closing a terminal tab is not a server error) + a server `handle_error` quiet-mixin + handler `log_error` override. Fixtures: race-proof teardown ordering. Verified flake-gone (5/5 then 3/3 repeated Playwright runs). Two follow-on regressions from the hardening were fixed: a distro high-entropy false-positive (reformatted a long exception-name run) and `test_single_instance`'s exact-type pin (faithfully adapted to `isinstance(ThreadingHTTPServer)` + not-exclusive â€” same discriminating intent).\n35\t- **GATE 2 (orchestrator-run, of record).** `python -m pytest -q` â†’ **GREEN 1102 passed, 1 skipped**; flake confirmed gone (3 stress runs + clean full run).\n36\t- **VERDICT: GO â€” committed to branch (9594d89).** âœ… **John signed off (\"carry on\", standing approval).** Wave 3 done.\n37\t\n38\t## Wave 4 â€” Grass archive + grassâ†’project lineage back-reference â€” âœ… GREEN (awaiting John's UI sign-off)\n39\t\n40\t- **EXECUTE.** `effort_history.archive_grass_session` (NEW verb: persist a dev session's docs via the v8 keystone + summary ref + per-idea `archives` bundle; idea stays in grass; distinct from save_refinement/export). `session_registry.grass_origin` field; `terminal_session.start_session` stamps/inherits it; `export_grass_to_project` stamps it. UI: per-lane Archive control + \"Archived material\" list + \"from grass:\" panel chip; SAFE projection carries grass_origin (never worktree/branch); NEW token-gated `POST /api/rnd/grass_archive`. Mockup + 14 tests.\n41\t- **GATE 1.** Full suite GREEN 1116.\n42\t- **REVIEW (2 independent, refute) â€” CONCERNS/lean-GO.** Reviewer A: archive/security/Playwright genuinely defended; LOW â€” grass_origin inheritance is one-level-deep (chip compensates by chain-walking, fragile for a board-tile field). Reviewer B: MEDIUM â€” mockup depicts a board-TILE chip not implemented (only panel); MEDIUM â€” dead chip when origin idea deleted (inert link); MEDIUM â€” archive not idempotent (double-click duplicates). Resolved coherently toward D8 (\"every downstream session traces back\" â†’ visible on the board).\n43\t- **FIX iter 1.** (1) grass_origin inheritance now reaches the **chain root** (bounded chain_members read) so every record carries the stamp â€” new transitive test fails pre-fix (non-vacuous). (2) Implemented the **board-tile chip** (SAFE-field stub resolved client-side; found+fixed the `\"plan\"` vs `\"planning\"` column-key bug) â€” reality now matches the mockup. (3) **Dead-chip** greyed/suppressed \"from grass (idea removed)\" with no live link (panel + tile). (4) **Idempotent archive** (content-addressed on lane+session+docs). (5) Mockup reconciled. Tests 11â†’21.\n44\t- **FLAKE STABILIZATION (systemic â€” protects all remaining gates).** Across 3 full runs the gate flaked on a different streaming test each time (WinError 10053, then a `PytestUnhandledThreadExceptionWarning` from an SSE pump's `ValueError(\"closed file\")` escaping the loop guards). Fix: `tests/conftest.py` autouse harness â€” a `threading.excepthook` that swallows ONLY benign daemon-thread teardown exceptions (the production `_is_benign_disconnect` set + \"closed file\" ValueError + reaped-session KeyError/RuntimeError) and DELEGATES real ones; + a reap fixture for leaked servers/threads. Product: `_sse_event` normalizes the `ValueError(\"closed file\")` â†’ BrokenPipeError so existing guards catch it. No assertion/feature changed. Verified: 2 full runs (agent) + 1 orchestrator run all GREEN 1123, + streaming cluster Ã—3 with warnings escalated to hard errors â€” deterministic.\n45\t- **GATE 2 (orchestrator-run, of record).** `python -m pytest -q` â†’ **GREEN 1123 passed, 1 skipped** (3rd consecutive clean full run).\n46\t- **VERDICT: GO â€” committed to branch (bcbd3ca).** âœ… **John signed off (\"carry on\", standing approval).** Wave 4 done.\n47\t\n48\t## Wave 5 â€” Grass researchâ†’plan live handoff (within the workbench, UI) â€” âœ… GREEN (awaiting John's UI sign-off)\n49\t\n50\t- **EXECUTE.** `effort_history.advance_grass_research_to_plan` â€” persists the research dev docs, builds the researchâ†’plan prompt (W2), starts/focuses the CONTAINED `(idea,'plan')` dev session linked + grass_origin-stamped + paste-pending (W1); honest-negative requires a REAL persisted research doc (no fabricated handoff). UI: \"âžœ Advance to Plan\" on the research terminal bar â†’ token-gated `POST /api/rnd/grass_advance` â†’ plan terminal toggles open with the pasted-unsent prompt. Mockup + 8 tests.\n51\t- **GATE 1.** Full suite GREEN 1131.\n52\t- **REVIEW (2 independent, refute) â€” CONCERNS, two real defects.** (1, â‰¥2 agree, B reproduced) develop-plan-FIRST â†’ Advance silently drops the handoff: the focus-existing branch returned the bare develop session without delivering the prompt, while the UI flashed \"prompt ready\" over an empty input. (2, Reviewer A, concrete repro) grass-dev sessions excluded from the board lane columns but NOT the top strip â†’ on reload/`repopulate()` the contained grass research/plan sessions leaked onto `#sessionBar` (pre-existing for develop; advance reproduces it). All else passed both (paste/no-submit, honest-negative, JS integrity, endpoint security, scope).\n53\t- **FIX iter 1.** (1) New `terminal_session.queue_paste(sid, text)` (W1 plumbing, internal guard) + deliver-on-focus iff `not pending_paste and not paste_flushed` (a bare develop session gets the handoff once; re-advance never double-pastes); `advanceGrassToPlan` flashes the hint only when `paste_delivered`. Non-vacuous (the ordering test fails pre-fix). (2) Top-strip containment: `term_sessions` projection now skips grass-dev labels (server) + a JS `repopulate()` skip (the `[grass-dev]` prefix injected once from the Python constant so they can't drift); the grass workbench still mounts its terminals by session id directly. Non-vacuous (the projection test fails with the filter disabled). Tests 10â†’13 (+ browser reload assertion that `#sessionBar` is grass-dev-free).\n54\t- **GATE 2 (orchestrator-run, of record).** `python -m pytest -q` â†’ **GREEN 1136 passed, 1 skipped**.\n55\t- **VERDICT: GO â€” committed to branch (e506859).** âœ… **John signed off (\"carry on\", standing approval).** Wave 5 done.\n56\t\n57\t## Wave 6 â€” Boneyard store + capture wiring (backend, NEW boneyard.py) â€” âœ… GREEN (backend; no UI sign-off)\n58\t\n59\t- **EXECUTE.** NEW stdlib `boneyard.py` â€” per-project index under `.anchor/projects/<id>/boneyard/` (index.json + entries/<id>.json, atomic under WRITE_LOCK): `record_entry` (content-addressed idempotent upsert) / `list_entries` / `search` (stdlib token-substring over title+summary+idea+doc paths) / `get_entry` + `build_session_entry` / `build_grass_entry`. Capture wired (all best-effort, never block the op): `kill`â†’`killed` (only w/ material), `delete_session`â†’`deleted` (BEFORE `delete_session_efforts` drops the pointers â€” D10),